Ethical Hacking in Termux
==========================

IMPORTANT LEGAL NOTICE
-----------------------
Only use these tools on systems you OWN or have WRITTEN PERMISSION to test.
Unauthorized access to systems is illegal in most countries and can result
in criminal charges. This guide is strictly for:
  - Learning on your own devices/networks
  - Authorized penetration testing engagements
  - CTF (Capture The Flag) competitions
  - Security research in controlled lab environments


========================================
SETUP & ESSENTIAL TOOLS
========================================

Update Termux first:
    pkg update && pkg upgrade

Install core dependencies:
    pkg install python python2 git curl wget nmap
    pkg install openssh openssl net-tools
    pkg install build-essential binutils


========================================
1. INFORMATION GATHERING
========================================

NMAP (Network Scanner)
-----------------------
    pkg install nmap

    nmap <target-ip>                    # basic scan
    nmap -sV <target-ip>               # service/version detection
    nmap -sV -O <target-ip>            # OS detection
    nmap -p 1-65535 <target-ip>        # scan all ports
    nmap -A <target-ip>                # aggressive scan (OS, version, scripts)
    nmap -sn 192.168.1.0/24            # ping sweep (find live hosts)
    nmap --script vuln <target-ip>     # vulnerability scripts

WHOIS LOOKUP
-------------
    pkg install whois
    whois example.com

DNS ENUMERATION
----------------
    pkg install dnsutils
    nslookup example.com               # basic DNS lookup
    dig example.com                    # detailed DNS info
    dig example.com MX                 # mail server records
    dig example.com ANY                # all records
    host -t ns example.com             # name servers

CURL FOR HTTP RECON
--------------------
    curl -I https://example.com        # HTTP headers only
    curl -v https://example.com        # verbose (shows full handshake)
    curl -L https://example.com        # follow redirects


========================================
2. WEB APPLICATION TESTING
========================================

INSTALL PYTHON TOOLS
---------------------
    pip install requests beautifulsoup4

SQLMAP (SQL Injection Testing)
-------------------------------
    pkg install python git
    git clone https://github.com/sqlmapproject/sqlmap.git
    cd sqlmap
    python3 sqlmap.py -u "http://target.com/page?id=1"
    python3 sqlmap.py -u "http://target.com/page?id=1" --dbs    # list databases
    python3 sqlmap.py -u "http://target.com/page?id=1" --dump   # dump data

NIKTO (Web Server Scanner)
---------------------------
    pkg install perl
    git clone https://github.com/sullo/nikto.git
    cd nikto/program
    perl nikto.pl -h http://target.com

DIRB / DIRECTORY BRUTEFORCE (Python alternative)
-------------------------------------------------
    pip install dirsearch
    python3 -m dirsearch -u http://target.com -e php,html,js

SUBDOMAIN ENUMERATION
----------------------
    pip install sublist3r
    python3 sublist3r.py -d example.com


========================================
3. PASSWORD TESTING
========================================

HYDRA (Login Brute Forcer)
---------------------------
    pkg install hydra

    # SSH brute force:
    hydra -l username -P wordlist.txt ssh://target-ip

    # FTP brute force:
    hydra -l admin -P wordlist.txt ftp://target-ip

    # HTTP login form:
    hydra -l admin -P wordlist.txt target.com http-post-form \
      "/login:username=^USER^&password=^PASS^:Invalid"

WORDLISTS
----------
    # Install SecLists (popular wordlist collection):
    git clone https://github.com/danielmiessler/SecLists.git

    # Common paths:
    SecLists/Passwords/Common-Credentials/10-million-password-list-top-1000.txt
    SecLists/Discovery/Web-Content/directory-list-2.3-medium.txt

HASH CRACKING (Hashcat alternative for Android)
-------------------------------------------------
    pip install hashid                 # identify hash type
    hashid '<hash-here>'

    # John the Ripper:
    pkg install john
    john --wordlist=wordlist.txt hashfile.txt
    john --show hashfile.txt           # show cracked passwords


========================================
4. NETWORK ANALYSIS
========================================

TCPDUMP (Packet Capture)
-------------------------
    pkg install tcpdump

    tcpdump -i wlan0                   # capture on wifi interface
    tcpdump -i wlan0 -w capture.pcap   # save to file
    tcpdump -i wlan0 port 80           # capture HTTP traffic
    tcpdump -i wlan0 host 192.168.1.1  # capture traffic to/from host

    # View interfaces:
    ip link show

NETCAT (Swiss Army Knife)
--------------------------
    pkg install netcat-openbsd

    nc -lvp 4444                       # listen on port 4444
    nc target-ip 4444                  # connect to target
    nc -zv target-ip 20-80             # port scan range

METASPLOIT (Advanced Framework)
---------------------------------
    # Install via unofficial Termux script:
    pkg install unstable-repo
    pkg install metasploit

    # Or manual install:
    curl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rapid7/metasploit-omnibus/master/config/templates/metasploit-framework-wrappers/msfupdate.erb > msfinstall
    chmod +x msfinstall
    ./msfinstall

    msfconsole                         # start Metasploit


========================================
5. WIRELESS SECURITY TESTING
========================================

Note: Wireless packet injection requires a compatible WiFi adapter.
Android's built-in WiFi chip usually doesn't support monitor mode.
Use an external USB WiFi adapter (via OTG cable).

    pkg install aircrack-ng

    airmon-ng start wlan0              # enable monitor mode
    airodump-ng wlan0mon               # scan for networks
    airodump-ng -c <channel> --bssid <AP_MAC> -w capture wlan0mon
    aircrack-ng -w wordlist.txt capture-01.cap


